  "interpretation": "R-squared on rupee value is high for every model including the zero-return baseline, because portfolio value at t+h is dominated by value at t plus contributions; it measures scale, not skill. Skill against the zero-return baseline is also flattering, because that baseline ignores market drift and so is biased low by roughly the average market return over the horizon. The honest figures are R-squared on excess log growth and the skill score against the mean-drift baseline, which are equivalent to each other and measure what a model adds over the best constant forecast."
